  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="f359-78b3-b6e7-f8fb" name="Ptolemaic Egyptian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #26 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). Ptolemy was the other great beneficiary of the successor wars, securing control of Egypt and ruling as Pharaoh. He was virtually the only one of Alexander’s generals to die in his bed. The state was eventually annexed as a province of Rome after its involvement in the wars that ended the Republic. 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Ptolemaic Egyptian]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  War Machines: up to 10%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 25% Infantry: At least 25% Elephants: 1 per 1000 points War Machines: Up to 10%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
